E=R/'explorations/dum-club-refinement'
G=json.loads((E/'sources/geometry.json').read_text())
body='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>The Dum Club, refined — Dum E Odisha</title><link rel="icon" href="../../assets/logo/favicon.png"><link rel="stylesheet" href="../explorations.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="club.css"><script src="club.js" defer></script></head><body><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to refinement</a><header class="topbar"><a class="brand" href="../../index.html">DUM E ODISHA</a><nav class="toplinks" aria-label="Refinement"><a href="#compare">Before & after</a><a href="#geometry">Golden ratio</a><a href="#applications">Brand world</a></nav></header><main class="wrap" id="main"><div class="intro"><p class="eyebrow">Your original idea / A focused refinement</p><h1>The Dum Club.<br>Same soul. Clearer form.</h1><p class="lead">The rounded lowercase name, raised lid, rice detail and warm palette stay. The spacing, counters and hierarchy get a more disciplined treatment.</p></div><div class="hero-refinement"><figure class="hero-mark"><img id="active-logo" src="assets/negative-space-primary.png" alt="Refined negative-space Dum E Odisha logo"></figure><div><span class="tag">Two refinements / one base idea</span><h2>A familiar mark,<br>made easier to read.</h2><p>The faithful version keeps the original grain detail. The negative-space version turns the d counter into a rice kernel and makes the lid opening clearer.</p><div class="variant-choices" role="group" aria-label="Choose refinement preview"><button type="button" data-variant="faithful" aria-pressed="false">Faithful refinement</button><button type="button" data-variant="negative-space" aria-pressed="true">Negative space</button></div><p class="small" id="variant-description">Negative space / the rice kernel is the counter, not an extra floating shape.</p><a id="active-download" href="assets/negative-space-primary.png" download>Download this transparent PNG ↓</a></div></div>
<section class="section" id="compare"><p class="eyebrow">01 / Continuity, not a new concept</p><h2>Keep the idea.<br>Remove the friction.</h2><div class="comparison-grid"><figure><img src="assets/owner-reference.png" alt="The exact original logo supplied by the owner"><figcaption>01 / Owner-supplied reference</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="assets/faithful-primary.png" alt="Faithful refinement with a clearer gap before e and shorter m terminal"><figcaption>02 / Faithful refinement</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="assets/negative-space-primary.png" alt="Negative-space refinement with a rice-shaped d counter"><figcaption>03 / Negative-space refinement</figcaption></figure></div><div class="two-col alignment-top"><div><h3>What stays</h3><ul><li>Soft lowercase d, u, m and the separate e.</li><li>The lifted lid integrated with the name.</li><li>Saffron, chilli and cream.</li><li>ODISHA as a readable part of the full name.</li></ul></div><div><h3>What changes</h3><ul><li>A visible gap separates m and e.</li><li>The long m flourish becomes a controlled terminal.</li><li>Cleaner counters and a simpler lid slit.</li><li>A measured name-line hierarchy and clearspace.</li></ul></div></div></section>
<section class="section" id="negative-space"><div class="two-col"><div><p class="eyebrow">02 / Let the empty space work</p><h2>The rice is<br>the counter.</h2><p>Instead of putting a separate golden grain inside the d, the empty counter becomes one kernel-like form. The tapered gap below the lid is the second negative-space cue.</p><p>This keeps the cooking idea inside the existing letter-and-lid construction. It does not add an unrelated monogram or another illustration above the name.</p><p class="note">The kernel cue is clearer in a generous one-ink rendering. At very small sizes, use a simpler compact mark developed from the chosen artwork rather than shrinking this whole name indefinitely.</p></div><div class="detail-grid"><figure><img src="proofs/rice-counter-detail.png" alt="Cropped proof of the rice-kernel negative space inside d"><figcaption>d counter / actual artwork crop</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="proofs/lid-detail.png" alt="Cropped proof of the cream opening under the lifted lid"><figcaption>Lid opening / actual artwork crop</figcaption></figure></div></div></section>
<section class="section" id="geometry"><p class="eyebrow">03 / A measured layout study</p><h2>A useful role<br>for the golden ratio.</h2><div class="two-col alignment-top"><div><p>φ = (1 + √5) / 2 ≈ 1.618034. The main-name image is 1000 px wide; ODISHA is 618 px wide. The export ratio is 1.618123 after whole-pixel rounding.</p><p>The line gap is 56 px, rounded from 1000/φ⁶. Clearspace is 90 px, rounded from 1000/φ⁵. Both versions use those same layout rules.</p><p class="note">These are real measurements of the delivered raster lockup. The generated letter contours are optically refined shapes; they are not claimed to be mathematically exact golden circles. A golden grid is a construction aid, not proof of beauty or originality.</p></div><div class="ratio-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Target / export</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Main-name width</td><td>1000 px</td></tr><tr><td>ODISHA width</td><td>1000/φ → 618 px</td></tr><tr><td>Name-line gap</td><td>1000/φ⁶ → 56 px</td></tr><tr><td>Clearspace</td><td>1000/φ⁵ → 90 px</td></tr><tr><td>Width ratio</td><td>1.618123</td></tr><tr><td>Rounding difference</td><td>0.0055% from φ</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><figure class="gallery-figure"><img class="image-full" src="proofs/phi-layout.png" alt="Measured golden-ratio layout showing the 1000-pixel main name and 618-pixel Odisha line"><figcaption>Measured placed-image bounds, with actual export dimensions and rounding.</figcaption></figure><div class="links"><a href="proofs/phi-layout.png" download>Download measured layout PNG ↓</a><a href="proofs/phi-layout.svg" download>Construction diagram SVG ↓</a><a href="sources/geometry.json">Exact measurements ↗</a></div><p class="small">The construction SVG contains the raster logo for annotation. It is not an editable-vector logo master.</p></section>
<section class="section" id="variants"><p class="eyebrow">04 / A practical family</p><h2>Colour, single ink<br>and after dark.</h2><figure class="gallery-figure"><img class="image-full" src="proofs/variants-and-sizes.png" alt="Two-ink, single-ink and reversed logo proofs, plus 240- and 180-pixel examples"><figcaption>Same source geometry and spacing across the exported variants.</figcaption></figure><div class="links"><a href="assets/negative-space-primary.png" download>Primary PNG ↓</a><a href="assets/negative-space-mono.png" download>Single-ink PNG ↓</a><a href="assets/negative-space-reversed.png" download>Reversed PNG ↓</a><a href="assets/faithful-primary.png" download>Faithful alternative PNG ↓</a></div><p class="note">Use the full logo at 240 px or more for everyday digital work. The 180 px proof is a smaller stress example, not a print minimum. Saffron stays in the artwork; use chilli or dark ink for practical text. Raster files need vector reconstruction and physical proofing before large signage.</p></section>
<section class="section" id="applications"><p class="eyebrow">05 / The brand, together</p><h2>A warm, recognisable<br>world around the mark.</h2><p>Quiet cream faces give the name space. Lid arcs and kernel shapes become supporting graphics. Saffron brings warmth; chilli carries clear text and a strong secondary field.</p><figure class="gallery-figure"><a href="assets/brand-system.png"><img class="image-full" src="assets/brand-system.webp" alt="Refined Dum Club identity applied to takeaway packaging, seals and supporting graphics"></a><figcaption>Generated packaging/brand concept. Applied lettering is illustrative; the downloadable standalone lockup is the canonical review reference.</figcaption></figure><a href="assets/brand-system.png" download>Download brand concept PNG ↓</a><h3 style="margin-top:45px">A wall with the same personality.</h3><figure class="gallery-figure"><a href="assets/wall-concept.png"><img class="image-full" src="assets/wall-concept.webp" alt="Generated restaurant-wall concept using the refined rounded logo and rice/lid mural graphics"></a><figcaption>Proposed interior, not a photograph of the operating business.</figcaption></figure><a href="assets/wall-concept.png" download>Download wall concept PNG ↓</a></section>
<section class="section" id="display"><p class="eyebrow">06 / A golden split on screen</p><h2>The layout rules<br>have a job to do.</h2><p>The TV holding slide divides the screen into φ:1 panels: a generous cream identity field and a quieter chilli message field. The logo remains the exact placed asset; supporting text is live and editable.</p><img class="image-full" src="assets/tv-display.png" width="1920" height="1080" alt="1920-by-1080 brand display with a golden-ratio panel split"><div class="links"><a href="assets/tv-display.png" download>TV PNG ↓</a><a href="tv-display.html">Open editable display ↗</a></div></section>
<section class="section"><p class="eyebrow">07 / Use it consistently</p><h2>Small rules.<br>A stronger identity.</h2><div class="two-col alignment-top"><div><h3>Keep fixed</h3><p>The rounded glyphs, d kernel, lid slit, visible gap before e and ODISHA line. Place the complete supplied asset, with its supplied clearspace. Keep the same counter shapes when developing a vector master.</p><h3>Let the supporting system flex</h3><p>Use broad lid arcs and kernel shapes on separate panels. Leave operational information on quiet cream or chilli areas. Keep the existing line “Flavour in Every Layer.” outside the small logo.</p></div><div><h3>Review recommendation</h3><p>Develop the negative-space version if the kernel counter and lid opening read well in real use. Retain the faithful version as the closer alternative to your original drawing. The owner has requested the exploration; neither outcome has been recorded as a final selection.</p><h3>Next production step</h3><p>Reconstruct clean vectors from the selected artwork, preserve the optical corrections, test one-ink counters at actual print size and obtain a physical proof. The generated PNGs and annotated diagram do not replace that stage.</p></div></div><div class="links"><a href="sources/generation-prompts.json">Prompts & provenance ↗</a><a href="../../../../brand/brand-concept-13-dum-club.html">Original Dum Club concept ↗</a><a href="../index.html">All other explorations ↗</a></div></section><footer><a href="../../index.html">Back to the main brand guide ←</a><span>Focused refinement / 17 October 2026 / owner review pending</span></footer></main></body></html>'''
(E/'index.html').write_text(body)
tv='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Dum Club / Editable golden-split TV display</title><style>*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:#e6d8c2;font:17px/1.5 Arial,sans-serif;color:#29231F}.toolbar{max-width:950px;margin:auto;padding:25px}.toolbar a{color:#A63825}button{padding:10px 18px;background:#A63825;color:#FFF3DD;border:0;font:inherit;cursor:pointer}.stage{padding:25px 0;overflow:auto}.canvas{width:1920px;height:1080px;margin:auto;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.61803398875fr 1fr;overflow:hidden}.identity{background:#FFF3DD;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center}.identity img{width:1000px;height:auto;max-width:90%}.message{background:#A63825;color:#FFF3DD;padding:110px 65px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:center}.message p{font-size:18px;letter-spacing:3px;text-transform:uppercase;margin:0 0 45px}.message h1{font:82px/1.1 Georgia,serif;margin:0 0 70px;letter-spacing:-2px}.message .details{font-size:23px;line-height:1.8;letter-spacing:0;text-transform:none;margin:0}a:focus-visible,button:focus-visible,[contenteditable]:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #ECAA35;outline-offset:4px}@media print{@page{size:1920px 1080px;margin:0}.toolbar{display:none}.stage{padding:0;overflow:visible}.canvas{margin:0;print-color-adjust:exact;-webkit-print-color-adjust:exact}}</style></head><body><div class="toolbar"><a href="index.html#display">← Back to the refinement</a><p>1920 × 1080 px / φ:1 panel split. Click the message to edit; inspect wrapping before export.</p><button type="button" onclick="window.print()">Print / save PDF proof</button></div><div class="stage"><article class="canvas"><div class="identity"><img src="assets/negative-space-primary.png" alt="Refined Dum E Odisha negative-space logo"></div><div class="message"><p>Dum E Odisha / Biryani</p><h1 contenteditable="true" aria-label="Editable brand headline">Flavour in<br>Every Layer.</h1><p class="details">Bhubaneswar<br>Bulk orders: +91 78942 65632<br>@dum_e_odisha</p></div></article></div></body></html>'''
(E/'tv-display.html').write_text(tv)
guide=R/'index.html';s=guide.read_text()
section='''<section id="dum-club-refinement"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">Latest / Your original Dum Club idea, refined</p><h2>Same soul.<br>Clearer form.</h2></div><p>Two focused refinements preserve the rounded name and lifted lid. Explore a rice-kernel counter, a real golden-ratio layout study, one-ink proofs and a coordinated brand world.</p></div><div class="idea-grid food-grid"><article class="idea-card"><a href="explorations/dum-club-refinement/index.html"><img src="explorations/dum-club-refinement/assets/negative-space-primary.png" alt="Refined Dum Club negative-space logo"><span>Negative space / golden-ratio layout</span><h3>The Dum Club, refined</h3><p>See before & after, geometry and brand applications ↗</p></a></article><article class="idea-card"><a href="explorations/dum-club-refinement/index.html#geometry"><img src="explorations/dum-club-refinement/proofs/phi-layout.png" alt="Measured 1000-to-618 golden-ratio name hierarchy"><span>Measured construction study</span><h3>The proportions, explained</h3><p>View actual dimensions and export proofs ↗</p></a></article></div></section>'''
if 'id="dum-club-refinement"' in s:s=re.sub(r'<section id="dum-club-refinement">.*?</section>',lambda _:section,s,count=1,flags=re.S)
else:s=s.replace('<main id="main">','<main id="main">'+section,1)
